= Foreword

Unlike the other subjects in this repo, I do have quite some background in physics, so this roadmap here is going to be more advanced compared to the others. Still, physics is a very broad subject, and obviously I don't every bit of physics. My goals for self studying physics are:
1. To revisit a lot of the grad school textbooks, including all the famous Landau's book
2. To learn about topics which I was not specialized in, such as plasma physics, nuclear fusion, quantum information, material science, string theory, etc.
3. Develop a high quality guide which serious science enjoyers can follow in their spare time. This is primarily targeting people like me, who is once an academic but decided to take up better occupations or follow their dream in life, and trying to convince people we can still enjoy science with significant depth even outside academia.

